      "idx": 0,
      "label": "1",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "The immediate aim is to reproduce a known\nlanguage-model learning recipe. Math gives\nus an answer we can check. Recursive\nchoices come later. This is a small\nreproduction, not a new method or a\nreproduction of the paper's headline\nscores."
    },
    {
      "idx": 1,
      "label": "2",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "This example is invented. The model\ngenerates its own attempts. The checker\nsupplies only final-answer scores.\nRelative scores guide weight updates. We\nuse eight attempts per question. If all\neight scores agree, there is no within-\nquestion learning signal."
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "label": "3",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "The main run started from the base model:\n512 questions, eight attempts each, 32\nupdates. The 128 test questions were\nexcluded from training and monitoring. We\ncannot rule out earlier pretraining\nexposure. No worked-solution SFT stage was\nadded."
    },
    {
      "idx": 3,
      "label": "4",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Fixed test: 41 to 80 correct out of 128.\nThere were 44 gains and five losses. Same\nprompts and checker. We used the final\ncheckpoint, not the best. This is one\ntraining run. More test questions cannot\nreplace an independent training repeat."
    },
    {
      "idx": 4,
      "label": "5",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Actual test row 5: repeated fraction\nquestion became a correct 0.15. Responses\nare summarized. Of 44 gains, 36 started as\ncapped responses. That describes the\nchange, not its cause. Prompt controls are\npending. Math gains do not establish\nbetter RLM decomposition."
    }
  ]
